{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FoWYc8CqCQx3K5Xk4FZFyA","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Architecture — Wood-Panel Cutting & Edge-Banding Order Platform (\"Panel-Ops\")\n2\t\n3\t**Version:** 1.0 · **Owner:** Architect AI · **Date:** 2026-07-17\n4\t**Status:** Approved baseline for Phase 0–3 execution. Changes require an ADR.\n5\t\n6\t---\n7\t\n8\t## 1. Architecture Summary\n9\t\n10\tInternal browser-based operational platform for a Colombian wood-panel SME (3 users).\n11\tSingle source of truth per customer order: intake → review → normalization → confirmation →\n12\tquotation → approval → payment verification → production handoff → delivery → closure.\n13\t\n14\tMVP stack (Decision D-01, see ADR-001):\n15\t\n16\t- **Frontend:** HTML + CSS + vanilla JavaScript, served by Apps Script Web App.\n17\t- **Backend:** Google Apps Script (Web App, `doGet`/`doPost` JSON API).\n18\t- **Data layer:** Google Sheets as logical tables with stable UUID-style IDs.\n19\t- **Documents:** Google Drive structured folders per order.\n20\t- **Identity:** Google Workspace accounts; role table in Sheets.\n21\t- **Automation:** Apps Script time-driven triggers (aging alerts); n8n later.\n22\t- **Messaging:** WhatsApp deep links with pre-filled templates; official API later.\n23\t- **Exports:** canonical part model + independent LEPTON / KDT adapters.\n24\t\n25\tDesign constraint: every schema, ID, and contract must survive a future migration to\n26\tPostgreSQL/Supabase without data rewrite (migration triggers in §8).\n27\t\n28\t## 2. Component Diagram\n29\t\n30\t```mermaid\n31\tflowchart TB\n32\t    subgraph Client [Browser - internal users]\n33\t        UI[SPA: Dashboard / Kanban / Ticket Detail / Part Editor / Quotation / Payments / Prices / Reports]\n34\t    end\n35\t    subgraph GAS [Google Apps Script Web App]\n36\t        API[JSON API layer]\n37\t        RULES[Business rules and validation]\n38\t        SM[Workflow state machine]\n39\t        PRICE[Pricing and snapshot engine]\n40\t        PDF[PDF generator]\n41\t        IMP[Import mapping engine CSV or XLSX]\n42\t        EXP[Export adapters LEPTON and KDT]\n43\t        DRIVE[Drive folder automation]\n44\t        ALERT[Aging trigger 1h alerts]\n45\t    end\n46\t    subgraph Data [Google Workspace]\n47\t        SHEETS[(Google Sheets logical tables)]\n48\t        GDRIVE[(Google Drive order case files)]\n49\t    end\n50\t    subgraph External\n51\t        WA[WhatsApp Business deep links]\n52\t        LEPTON[LEPTON optimizer]\n53\t        KDT[KDT optimizer]\n54\t        QT[Existing web quotation tool - future route D]\n55\t    end\n56\t    UI --> API --> RULES --> SHEETS\n57\t    RULES --> SM\n58\t    RULES --> PRICE\n59\t    API --> PDF --> GDRIVE\n60\t    API --> IMP\n61\t    API --> EXP --> LEPTON\n62\t    EXP --> KDT\n63\t    API --> DRIVE --> GDRIVE\n64\t    ALERT --> SHEETS\n65\t    UI -.pre-filled links.-> WA\n66\t    QT -.future.-> API\n67\t```\n68\t\n69\tGovernance plane (separate from the product):\n70\t\n71\t```mermaid\n72\tflowchart LR\n73\t    ARCH[Architect AI] -->|writes| RM[roadmap.md]\n74\t    DASH[GOV-001 dashboard localhost] -->|reads| RM\n75\t    DASH -->|spawns| EXEC[Executor agents claude or codex]\n76\t    EXEC -->|write| LEDGER[roadmap-status.md + logs/ + comments/]\n77\t    ARCH -->|reads evidence| LEDGER\n78\t```\n79\t\n80\t## 3. Bounded Contexts / Modules\n81\t\n82\t| Context | Responsibility | Key tables |\n83\t|---|---|---|\n84\t| **Intake** | Ticket creation, channel capture, immutable original source | Tickets, Imports, Documents |\n85\t| **Customer** | Customer master data | Customers |\n86\t| **Parts** | Canonical part schema, validation, editor, import mapping | Parts, Imports |\n87\t| **Workflow** | State machine, transitions, ownership, aging, labels | Tickets, Workflow_States, Activity |\n88\t| **Pricing** | Price tables, effective dating, snapshots | Panel_Prices, Cut_Prices, Edge_Banding_Prices, Configuration |\n89\t| **Quotation** | Quotation versions, lines, PDF, 48h validity | Quotations, Quotation_Lines |\n90\t| **Payments** | Registration, evidence, verification, commercial lock | Payments |\n91\t| **Documents** | Drive case file, naming convention, links | Documents |\n92\t| **Production Handoff** | Technical package, optimizer exports (price-free) | Parts, Documents |\n93\t| **Reporting** | KPIs, conversion, times, loss reasons | Activity + all |\n94\t| **Governance** | roadmap, dashboard, executor evidence (not part of product) | filesystem artifacts |\n95\t\n96\tCross-context rule: contexts communicate only through table contracts defined in\n97\t`data-model.md`. No module reads another module's internals.\n98\t\n99\t## 4. Integration Boundaries\n100\t\n101\t| Boundary | Contract | Direction | Status |\n102\t|---|---|---|---|\n103\t| LEPTON | CSV/XLSX file, layout TBD (DIS-001) | export only | **blocked on real sample** |\n104\t| KDT Optimizer | CSV/XLSX file, layout TBD (DIS-001) | export only | **blocked on real sample** |\n105\t| WhatsApp (phase 1) | `wa.me` deep link + URL-encoded template text | outbound, human sends | designable now |\n106\t| WhatsApp API (future) | official Business API | bidirectional | out of MVP |\n107\t| Existing quotation tool | Route D, contract TBD (DIS-002) | inbound | discovery |\n108\t| Bank email parsing | n8n, future | inbound | out of MVP |\n109\t\n110\tCore platform never depends on external file layouts — adapters only\n111\t(`integration-contracts.md`).\n112\t\n113\t## 5. Document Repository Structure\n114\t\n115\tAs specified in master doc §12 (root `/WOOD_PANEL_OPERATIONS`, per-order folders\n116\t`00_ORIGINAL_REQUEST` … `07_CLOSURE`, naming `ORD-YYYYMM-NNNN_*`). The Drive automation\n117\tmodule is the only writer of folder structure. Original request files: write-once —\n118\tthe app never overwrites or deletes anything in `00_ORIGINAL_REQUEST`.\n119\t\n120\t## 6. Security & Data-Integrity Invariants\n121\t\n122\t1. Access restricted to company Google Workspace accounts; role resolved server-side from `Users` table on every request. Client-side role checks are cosmetic only.\n123\t2. Original request artifacts immutable (write-once folder + Documents row flagged `immutable=true`).\n124\t3. All dimensions stored in millimetres; conversion at intake, never at read time.\n125\t4. Every quotation version stores a full price snapshot (denormalized into Quotation_Lines).\n126\t5. Paid order → commercial snapshot frozen; server rejects edits to Parts/Quotation of a paid ticket except through the authorized exception flow (management approval recorded in Activity).\n127\t6. Only role `billing` can set payment state to `confirmed`.\n128\t7. No transition to `Ready for production` without `Payment confirmed` (state machine enforced server-side).\n129\t8. Production exports must contain zero commercial fields — export adapters whitelist technical columns, never blacklist.\n130\t9. Every state change appends an Activity row: timestamp, user, from-state, to-state, note. Activity is append-only.\n131\t10. IDs are generated server-side, opaque, and stable (`CUS-`, `ORD-`, `PRT-`, `QUO-`, `PAY-` prefixes + sequence); never reused.\n132\t11. Sheets rows are never physically deleted — `status=inactive`/`deleted_at` soft-delete only.\n133\t12. AI agents (future) produce drafts only; cannot confirm prices, payments, or ambiguous dimensions.\n134\t13. Governance: `roadmap.md` read-only for executors and dashboard; runtime truth lives in `roadmap-status.md`.\n135\t\n136\t## 7. Non-Functional Requirements\n137\t\n138\t- 3 concurrent users, ~10–50 tickets/day assumed (unvalidated — DIS-003).\n139\t- Page interactions < 3 s perceived (Apps Script cold starts mitigated by single-page UI + batched reads).\n140\t- All writes go through a single Apps Script lock (`LockService`) to protect Sheets from concurrent corruption.\n141\t- Spanish UI text; English code identifiers and docs.\n142\t\n143\t## 8. Migration Triggers (to PostgreSQL/Supabase)\n144\t\n145\t>10 active users · >~20k tickets · multi-branch · automated banking · audit demands ·\n146\tmulti-tenant productization. Schema in `data-model.md` is written relationally to make\n147\tthis a data-copy, not a redesign.\n148\t\n149\t## 9. Architecture Deliverables Index\n150\t\n151\t- `architecture.md` (this file)\n152\t- `data-model.md`\n153\t- `workflow-state-machine.md`\n154\t- `permissions-matrix.md`\n155\t- `integration-contracts.md`\n156\t- `risk-register.md`\n157\t- `acceptance-strategy.md`\n158\t- `roadmap.md`\n159\t- `docs/adr/ADR-001-google-workspace-stack.md`\n160\t- `docs/adr/ADR-002-sheets-as-relational-store.md`\n161\t- `docs/adr/ADR-003-execution-governance.md`\n162\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2ba010ed-03ac-469a-a8dc-1e3686220e8a","uuid":"fa5873bd-4f92-459d-9c71-3bb387c692f0","timestamp":"2026-07-22T13:48:05.378Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/work945/Documents/Proyectos/ABM/proyectos/panel-ops/architecture.md","content":"# Architecture — Wood-Panel Cutting & Edge-Banding Order Platform (\"Panel-Ops\")\n\n**Version:** 1.0 · **Owner:** Architect AI · **Date:** 2026-07-17\n**Status:** Approved baseline for Phase 0–3 execution. Changes require an ADR.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Architecture Summary\n\nInternal browser-based operational platform for a Colombian wood-panel SME (3 users).\nSingle source of truth per customer order: intake → review → normalization → confirmation →\nquotation → approval → payment verification → production handoff → delivery → closure.\n\nMVP stack (Decision D-01, see ADR-001):\n\n- **Frontend:** HTML + CSS + vanilla JavaScript, served by Apps Script Web App.\n- **Backend:** Google Apps Script (Web App, `doGet`/`doPost` JSON API).\n- **Data layer:** Google Sheets as logical tables with stable UUID-style IDs.\n- **Documents:** Google Drive structured folders per order.\n- **Identity:** Google Workspace accounts; role table in Sheets.\n- **Automation:** Apps Script time-driven triggers (aging alerts); n8n later.\n- **Messaging:** WhatsApp deep links with pre-filled templates; official API later.\n- **Exports:** canonical part model + independent LEPTON / KDT adapters.\n\nDesign constraint: every schema, ID, and contract must survive a future migration to\nPostgreSQL/Supabase without data rewrite (migration triggers in §8).\n\n## 2. Component Diagram\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TB\n    subgraph Client [Browser - internal users]\n        UI[SPA: Dashboard / Kanban / Ticket Detail / Part Editor / Quotation / Payments / Prices / Reports]\n    end\n    subgraph GAS [Google Apps Script Web App]\n        API[JSON API layer]\n        RULES[Business rules and validation]\n        SM[Workflow state machine]\n        PRICE[Pricing and snapshot engine]\n        PDF[PDF generator]\n        IMP[Import mapping engine CSV or XLSX]\n        EXP[Export adapters LEPTON and KDT]\n        DRIVE[Drive folder automation]\n        ALERT[Aging trigger 1h alerts]\n    end\n    subgraph Data [Google Workspace]\n        SHEETS[(Google Sheets logical tables)]\n        GDRIVE[(Google Drive order case files)]\n    end\n    subgraph External\n        WA[WhatsApp Business deep links]\n        LEPTON[LEPTON optimizer]\n        KDT[KDT optimizer]\n        QT[Existing web quotation tool - future route D]\n    end\n    UI --> API --> RULES --> SHEETS\n    RULES --> SM\n    RULES --> PRICE\n    API --> PDF --> GDRIVE\n    API --> IMP\n    API --> EXP --> LEPTON\n    EXP --> KDT\n    API --> DRIVE --> GDRIVE\n    ALERT --> SHEETS\n    UI -.pre-filled links.-> WA\n    QT -.future.-> API\n```\n\nGovernance plane (separate from the product):\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n    ARCH[Architect AI] -->|writes| RM[roadmap.md]\n    DASH[GOV-001 dashboard localhost] -->|reads| RM\n    DASH -->|spawns| EXEC[Executor agents claude or codex]\n    EXEC -->|write| LEDGER[roadmap-status.md + logs/ + comments/]\n    ARCH -->|reads evidence| LEDGER\n```\n\n## 3. Bounded Contexts / Modules\n\n| Context | Responsibility | Key tables |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Intake** | Ticket creation, channel capture, immutable original source | Tickets, Imports, Documents |\n| **Customer** | Customer master data | Customers |\n| **Parts** | Canonical part schema, validation, editor, import mapping | Parts, Imports |\n| **Workflow** | State machine, transitions, ownership, aging, labels | Tickets, Workflow_States, Activity |\n| **Pricing** | Price tables, effective dating, snapshots | Panel_Prices, Cut_Prices, Edge_Banding_Prices, Configuration |\n| **Quotation** | Quotation versions, lines, PDF, 48h validity | Quotations, Quotation_Lines |\n| **Payments** | Registration, evidence, verification, commercial lock | Payments |\n| **Documents** | Drive case file, naming convention, links | Documents |\n| **Production Handoff** | Technical package, optimizer exports (price-free) | Parts, Documents |\n| **Reporting** | KPIs, conversion, times, loss reasons | Activity + all |\n| **Governance** | roadmap, dashboard, executor evidence (not part of product) | filesystem artifacts |\n\nCross-context rule: contexts communicate only through table contracts defined in\n`data-model.md`. No module reads another module's internals.\n\n## 4. Integration Boundaries\n\n| Boundary | Contract | Direction | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| LEPTON | CSV/XLSX file, layout TBD (DIS-001) | export only | **blocked on real sample** |\n| KDT Optimizer | CSV/XLSX file, layout TBD (DIS-001) | export only | **blocked on real sample** |\n| WhatsApp (phase 1) | `wa.me` deep link + URL-encoded template text | outbound, human sends | designable now |\n| WhatsApp API (future) | official Business API | bidirectional | out of MVP |\n| Existing quotation tool | Route D, contract TBD (DIS-002) | inbound | discovery |\n| Bank email parsing | n8n, future | inbound | out of MVP |\n\nCore platform never depends on external file layouts — adapters only\n(`integration-contracts.md`).\n\n## 5. Document Repository Structure\n\nAs specified in master doc §12 (root `/WOOD_PANEL_OPERATIONS`, per-order folders\n`00_ORIGINAL_REQUEST` … `07_CLOSURE`, naming `ORD-YYYYMM-NNNN_*`). The Drive automation\nmodule is the only writer of folder structure. Original request files: write-once —\nthe app never overwrites or deletes anything in `00_ORIGINAL_REQUEST`.\n\n## 6. Security & Data-Integrity Invariants\n\n1. Access restricted to company Google Workspace accounts; role resolved server-side from `Users` table on every request. Client-side role checks are cosmetic only.\n2. Original request artifacts immutable (write-once folder + Documents row flagged `immutable=true`).\n3. All dimensions stored in millimetres; conversion at intake, never at read time.\n4. Every quotation version stores a full price snapshot (denormalized into Quotation_Lines).\n5. Paid order → commercial snapshot frozen; server rejects edits to Parts/Quotation of a paid ticket except through the authorized exception flow (management approval recorded in Activity).\n6. Only role `billing` can set payment state to `confirmed`.\n7. No transition to `Ready for production` without `Payment confirmed` (state machine enforced server-side).\n8. Production exports must contain zero commercial fields — export adapters whitelist technical columns, never blacklist.\n9. Every state change appends an Activity row: timestamp, user, from-state, to-state, note. Activity is append-only.\n10. IDs are generated server-side, opaque, and stable (`CUS-`, `ORD-`, `PRT-`, `QUO-`, `PAY-` prefixes + sequence); never reused.\n11. Sheets rows are never physically deleted — `status=inactive`/`deleted_at` soft-delete only.\n12. AI agents (future) produce drafts only; cannot confirm prices, payments, or ambiguous dimensions.\n13. Governance: `roadmap.md` read-only for executors and dashboard; runtime truth lives in `roadmap-status.md`.\n\n## 7. Non-Functional Requirements\n\n- 3 concurrent users, ~10–50 tickets/day assumed (unvalidated — DIS-003).\n- Page interactions < 3 s perceived (Apps Script cold starts mitigated by single-page UI + batched reads).\n- All writes go through a single Apps Script lock (`LockService`) to protect Sheets from concurrent corruption.\n- Spanish UI text; English code identifiers and docs.\n\n## 8. Migration Triggers (to PostgreSQL/Supabase)\n\n>10 active users · >~20k tickets · multi-branch · automated banking · audit demands ·\nmulti-tenant productization. Schema in `data-model.md` is written relationally to make\nthis a data-copy, not a redesign.\n\n## 9. Architecture Deliverables Index\n\n- `architecture.md` (this file)\n- `data-model.md`\n- `workflow-state-machine.md`\n- `permissions-matrix.md`\n- `integration-contracts.md`\n- `risk-register.md`\n- `acceptance-strategy.md`\n- `roadmap.md`\n- `docs/adr/ADR-001-google-workspace-stack.md`\n- `docs/adr/ADR-002-sheets-as-relational-store.md`\n- `docs/adr/ADR-003-execution-governance.md`\n","numLines":162,"startLine":1,"totalLines":162}}}
